<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Revolt of the Brotherhoods</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1523">1523</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Germanies</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Revolt of the Brotherhoods, or Germanies, was a rising of the craft <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guilds</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> and other towns of the kingdom against the nobility between 1519 and 1523. Armed brotherhoods formed to defend the coast took control of the city and fought the nobles and their Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, many of whom the rebels forcibly baptised. Royal and noble forces crushed the revolt, and a similar rising on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Mallorca</a> was put down in 1523.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-brotherhoods.jpg" alt="Revolt of the Brotherhoods" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcelino de Unceta · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gerpaz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
